# el++ engine fixture 37 (src/test.slop: test-ksc-g-stops-at-bottom).
# K3: phase G stops committing at a round's first ⊥. a is an A after round 1,
# a B and a C after round 2. In round 3 the conclusions arrive in this order:
# from inst(a, B), inst(a, F) and then ⊥ (B ⊓ C ⊑ ⊥, with inst(a, C) already
# stored); from inst(a, C), inst(a, G). G stores inst(a, F) and stops at the
# ⊥, so inst(a, G) is never stored.
# Expect: inconsistent.
# Inside el++ whole: the engine must answer every class as the literal Psc
# reference does (test-ksc-engine-matches-reference).

@prefix : <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :F a owl:Class . :G a owl:Class .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual , :A .
:A rdfs:subClassOf :B , :C .
:B rdfs:subClassOf :F .
:C rdfs:subClassOf :G .
[ owl:intersectionOf ( :B :C ) ] rdfs:subClassOf owl:Nothing .
